# 1. Windows File Paths

A file path identifies the location of a file or folder.

### Local Windows Path

Example:

```text
C:\Users\John\Documents\report.txt
```

This represents a resource stored on the local computer.

### Network UNC Path

UNC stands for **Universal Naming Convention**.

A UNC path is a standard Windows path used to access a shared resource over a network without requiring a mapped drive letter.

Example:

```text
\\Server01\Finance\Reports
```

Structure:

```text
\\ServerName\ShareName\Folder\File
```

A server can also be referenced by IP address:

```text
\\192.168.1.10\Finance
```

### Important Distinction

```text
Local Path
↓
C:\Users\John\Documents

UNC Path
↓
\\Server01\Finance

Mapped Network Drive
↓
Z:\Finance
```

A mapped drive can point to a UNC path.

